    {
      "id": "claim_8316bc6c46c74f599049c10a518f190e",
      "statement": "The entrypoint updates /etc/zm/secrets.ini by replacing https://portal/ with http://zoneminder/, setting ZM_USER and ZM_PASSWORD from env, and generating a fresh 32-byte base64 MLAPI_SECRET_KEY via openssl rand -base64 32 on every startup — updating an existing line or appending one — so the ML API key rotates at each container start.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoint.sh#L104-L113",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfdeadd8e5afaee7f374531a1a9bbfac5300848fa7d7c210afa72af564130512:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_76d8cb82613942ddaeefba7e349ee341",
      "statement": "In the normal startup path the `exec \"$@\"` handoff after the DB phase is a no-op that falls through: the image declares ENTRYPOINT [\"entrypoint.sh\"] with no CMD, so $@ is empty and bash's bare exec continues the script into the zm.conf rewrites, MQTT/secrets.ini configuration, service starts, and the tail -f /dev/null keep-alive. Only when the container is started with a command override (docker run / docker-compose run / command:) does exec replace the shell, skipping all later blocks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L153-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d54129c33dd37bceb21054dbc0e0d017ec5864f31f67f30c6803d3465024e61:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://entrypoint.sh#L66-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa3f6b18f0ad225ef5435b5e3e13dc315489052c353a738223ab02015530caa6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_900cae83be2f4cc0bd7be975d626ae97",
      "statement": "The ML API (python3 /usr/src/app/mlapi/mlapi.py) and the event notification server (./zmeventnotification.pl) startup lines in entrypoint.sh are commented out rather than unreachable — they are inert code that never runs inside this container, and those components must be run as separate containers/processes.",
